            <ArticleTitle>Zieve's syndrome a potential surgical pitfall?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Zieve's syndrome consists of transient haemolytic anaemic, jaundice, hyperlipidaemia and alcohol-induced liver disease. It is rare with less than 75 cases reported in a Medicine literature search from 1966. It can present acutely with abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
